[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Range compilation violates the parse_range contract requiring acceptance of optional whitespace between relational/prefix operators and their targets: _CLAUSE_TOKEN_PATTERN (line 37) splits a clause on whitespace in _compile_clause (lines 289-300), so for input '>= 1.0.0' the standalone token '>=' is re-tokenized as operator '>' plus operand '=', which _expand_comparator then passes to _parse_target and rejects with InvalidRangeError 'Malformed version or wildcard expression'. Expected postcondition: '>= 1.0.0' is equivalent to '>=1.0.0' and must yield a satisfied >=1.0.0 comparator rather than raising InvalidRangeError; the same whitespace tolerance must hold for all relational and prefix operators (^, ~, <, <=, >, !=, =) and for wildcard targets such as '>= 1.x'.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Fix parse_range whitespace tolerance: _compile_clause now consumes a standalone whitespace-delimited relational/prefix operator (>=, <=, <, >, =, ==, !=, ^, ~) together with the next token before regex peeling, so '>= 1.0.0' and '>= 1.x' parse identically to their compact forms instead of splitting into '>' + '=' and raising InvalidRangeError
